safe backup iv's
a crash while a removed partition is wiped: the wipe is resumed when it is
opened again, until then its last two indices are not protected (see
Removing a partition in the README)
opening a partition reads the index of every macroblock of the base device,
that is slow for large base devices
the paranoia level is not stored: what is written before it is switched
(after a start) is written in level 1, scubed3ctl could warn when a partition
is mounted in level 0 or 1
